# atomic sandbox scene v1
# Hydrogen sulfide: S-H 1.336 Angstrom (2.5247 Bohr), H-S-H 92.11 degrees. NIST CCCBDB, experimental geometry
# (rSH, aHSH; Cook, De Lucia & Helminger, J. Mol. Struct. 28, 237 (1975)), converted at 1 Angstrom = 1.8897261 Bohr.
# The file carries no `ionic` line (the presets are the files as written): the app starts it under its default
# policy, cores only, where the Z > 10 atom is a generated pseudopotential on its valence grid. Under
# `--ionic none` the heavy nucleus is a Gaussian at sigma = h (Z sigma ~ 2.4 at h = 0.15): qualitatively wrong, not a
# useful run. 14 Bohr box at 57 x 0.25 as written (the Accurate default re-grids it to 95^3 x 0.15, same box).
grid 57 0.25
charge 0
nucleus 16  0      0      0
nucleus 1   1.8178 1.752  0
nucleus 1  -1.8178 1.752  0
